# What must never enter the image.
#
# Without this file, `docker build` sends the entire project directory to the
# daemon -- including data/, which on a working install holds every uploaded
# document, the Chroma index, and the SQLite database. That would bake one
# machine's private library into a shareable image and, on a public deploy,
# serve it to strangers. It also masks the volume mount: files baked at /app/data
# are shadowed at runtime, so the library appears to vanish rather than fail
# loudly.

# --- Runtime state (the important one) ------------------------------------- #
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite3

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------- #
# .env is read from the environment at runtime, never copied in. Baking it would
# put an API key inside a layer that anyone who pulls the image can read.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Virtualenvs ----------------------------------------------------------- #
# A host .venv is built for the host's OS and CPU. Copying a macOS venv into a
# linux/amd64 image produces binaries that cannot load at all.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Python bytecode ------------------------------------------------------- #
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# --- Tests and tooling ----------------------------------------------------- #
# Not shipped: the suite runs in CI and locally, not in the deployed container.
tests/
scripts/
.pytest_cache/
pytest.ini
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/

# --- Git and CI ------------------------------------------------------------ #
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# --- Docs and deploy config ------------------------------------------------ #
# Read by humans and by flyctl on the host, never by the running app.
README.md
DEPLOY.md
Makefile
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
fly.toml

# --- Editors, OS, caches --------------------------------------------------- #
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
node_modules/
.cache/
models/
